OK. I take the bait. This is straight from the source:

The way I see it there are several ways to wake up monster(s):

1. By directly setting msleeping to zero,
2. by calling wakeup() with pointer to the monster to be woken,
3. by calling wake_nearby(),
4. by calling wake_nearto() with coordinates and distance,
5. by calling disturb() with a pointer to a monster,
6. by calling awaken_monsters() with a distance and
7. by calling aggravate().

So here goes:

1. Directly setting msleeping to zero:
- When hero leashes a pet it is woken up.
- Cursed monster detection (crystal ball or potion) causes detected 
monsters to wake up.
- Entering Ludios wakes up all monsters on the level as long as Croesus 
lives.
- Created familiar is woken up if created sleeping.
- If kicked gold hits a shopkeeper, a priest, a mercenary or a monster 
that likes gold, it is woken up.
- Thrown object wakes up the monster it 'hits' even if it misses.
- A sleeping monster in the chain position is woken if the ball moves.
- The quest leader is woken if the quest artifact is thrown at the leader.
- If thrown food doesn't tame the monster it hit the monster is woken up.
- The water nymph created by a fountain is woken up if created asleep 
(like nymphs normally are created).
- If held by a sleeping monster there is chance that it is woken up when 
you try to move.
- If you frighten your pet while trying to untrap it it is woken up as 
it goes wild.
- If undetected monster is noticed in the same space as the hero it is 
woken up.
- When entering a court, a swamp, a morgue or a zoo, there is 1 in 3 
chance for each monster on that level to wake up unless the hero is stealthy
- The ants or snakes created by the clerical spell are woken up if 
created sleeping.
- When a monster hits another monster the defender is woken up even if 
the hit misses.
- The defender is also woken up if it was struck in monster to monster 
melee and is still alive. Why twice I cannot say.
- Angered guard are woken up. Guards can be angered in town:
	- By digging doors, trees, walls or fountains.
	- By kicking doors.
	- By robbing a shop.
	- By drying up fountains.
	- By picking locks.
	- If Kops are called.
	- If Kops would have been called but they are not compiled in.
	- By damaging peacefull priests, shopkeepers or guards.
	- In certain cases where you damage shop goods.
- Gurads can be angered in other places also:
	- By freeing prisoners on the quest.
- Mindflayers wake up those monsters that they damage by their brain 
sucking unless the monster is killed.
- When monster throws an item and it hits another monster the defender 
is woken up.
- If monster uses wand of striking, teleportation or cancellation or 
spell of cancellation and hits another monster the defender is woken up.
- If that teleportation wand hits a priest in temple the priest is woken 
up. Why twice I cannot say.
- If you calm nymphs they are woken up and made peaceful.
- If a monster plays a bugle soldiers on the level are woken up.
- If you improvise on a bugle soldiers on the level are woken up.
- If a potion hits a monster and doesn't anger it, it is woken up.
- Turning undeads wake up undead and demons (the latter if your level is 
high enough.)
- Priests in temples are woken if created asleep.
- If you chat with a sleeping priest the priest is woken up.
- If you read a scroll of scare monsters while confused or the scroll is 
cursed monsters on the level are woken up.
- The shopkeeper is woken up if:
	- His shop is robbed.
	- You try to pay.
	- Before bones are saved.
	- You try to sell something.
- Your steed is woken up if you kick it.
- If you try to help monster out of a trap it is woken up.
- If you attack a sleeping monster it is woken up.
- If you photograph a monster the flash wakes it up.
- When a werecreature transforms it wakes up.
- If the Wizard of Yendor is sleeping on the same lavel as the hero 
there is 1 in 40 chance every turn that he is woken up.
- When the Wizard of Yendor rearrives he might get woken up. The chance 
that he isn't woken up is 1 in the number of turns he last moved +1. Why 
+1, it's pretty slim anyways.
- Then he is woken up anyway. Once again there is no sense in the code.
- Explosion wakes up monsters on its radius (3x3).
- Various wands, spells and breaths no matter if they are originating 
from the hero or a monster wake up monsters that are on the path or at 
terminus.

2. wakeup() This function wakes the monster, makes it stop eating, sets 
it angry, reveals mimics and undetects hiders. It is called if:
- You wrap your bullwhip around a monster when trying to get out of a pit.
- You grap a monsters weapon with a bullwhip.
- Kicked gold hits a monster that is not a shopkeeper, a priest a 
mercenary or monster that likes gold.
- When flying through the air and bumping into a monster.
- Thrown object misses the target monster (1 in 3 chance).
- Thrown object hits the swallower.
- For all monsters on the earthquake radius.
- A potion hits a monster and angers it. Not angering just wakes up. 
Check above.
- A priest is angered.
- Attack an unseen monster.
- Undetected monsters or mimicing mimics are sensed.
- Monster is hit.
- Monster is missed in melee.
- Hero is polyed and attacking the defending monster with: kick, bite, 
sting, touch, butt, tentacle, hug, explosion or engulfing.
- You stumble onto a mimic.
- Hero hits a monster by wand of striking, slow monster, speed monster, 
polymorph, cancellation, teleportation, make invisible, light or spell 
of force bolt, drain life, slow monster, polymorph, cancellation, 
teleportation, stone to flesh if it hits a stone golem or potion of 
polymorph.

3. wake_nearby() This function sets msleeping to zero for all monsters 
that are inside the square of the radius 20 times the heros level. It 
also sets tame monsters and minions whistletime. It is called if:
- Hero uses a tin whistle.
- Half the time when hero uses a cursed magic whistle.
- Hero uses a bell or cursed Bell of Opening.
- Hero uses non-cursed Bell of Opening for the invocation.
- Hero digs down on a pool (of lava).
- Hero uses pickaxe against ironbars.
- Hero kicks succesfully (direction is asked) unless swallowed or 
levitating.
- Chest is forced open with a blunt weapon.
- Hero fumbles.
- Hero walks over squeaky board.
- Chest trap explodes.
- Boobytrapped door or tin explodes.

4. wake_nearto() This function set msleeping to zero for all monsters 
inside a radius from given locus. The locus and the radius (which is 
actually the square of the radius) are given in the call, which is done if:
- A drawbridge is destroyed. Locus: the drawbridge, radius: 500.
- The Bell of Opening opens a boobytrapped door. Locus: the door, 
radius: 121.
- Hero pushes a boulder into a pool. Locus: the pool, radius: 40.
- An explosion happens. Locus: explosion epicenter, radius: at least 50.
- A door was hit by wand of striking or spell of force bolt. Locus: the 
door, radius: 20, 40 if the door was trapped.
- A monster explodes. Locus: the monster, radius: 49.
- A monster open a boobytrapped door. Locus: the monster, radius: 40.
- A pet growls. Locus: the pet, radius: 18*the pets level.
- A pet yelps. Locus the pet, radius: 12*the pets level.
- A pet whimpers. Locus: the pet, radius: 6*the pets level.
- A werecreature howls. Locus: the werecreature, radius: 121.
- A giant shouts: "Fee Fie Foe Foo!" Locus: the giant, radius: 49.
- A land mine blows up. Locus: the land mine, radius: 400.
- A boulder hits another boulder. Locus: the hit position, radius 100.
- A monster steps on a squeky board. Locus: the monster, radius: 40.

5. disturb() This function is called when a sleeping monster gets it's 
move and it sets msleeping to zero if the monster is in:
- direct LOS		AND
- within 10 squares	AND
- hero is not stealthy or (the monster is an ettin and 9/10) AND
- (the monster is not a nymph, a jabberwock or a leprechaun) or 1/50 AND
- hero aggravates or (the monster is a dog or a human) or (1/7 and the 
monster is not mimicing furniture or object).

6. awaken_monsters() This function sets msleeping and mfrozen to zero 
and may frighten the monsters. The monsters affected are within a radius 
of the hero. The radius is given as the square of the radius. The 
function is called if:
- Hero improvises with tooled horn. Radius: 30*hero's level.
- Hero uses a drum of earthquake. Radius: the whole level.
- Hero uses a leather drum. Radius: 40*her's level.

7. aggravate() This function sets msleeping to zero to all the monsters 
on the level. It is called if:
- Hero is polyed into a shrieker and uses it's monster ability.
- A monster casts a wizard spell aggravate.
- A shrieker shrieks.
- Hero drinks a cursed potion of invisibility.
- Hero prays when polyed into a demon or undead and is not chaotic.
- Hero prays in the Gehennom.
- Hero sits on a throne with negative luck (one possible outcome).
- Hero reads a (un)cursed spellbook (one possible outcome).
- Carrying The amulet once in a while.

