P.S. NetHack treats distances as squares because there is no need to 
take the root. If a>=0 and b>=0 then if a>b then a^2>b^2.

So comparing the distance between two squares (x1,y1) and (x2,y2) 
against given measure z, one calculates (x1-x2)^2+(y1-y2)^2 and compares 
it with z^2

